  "notes": "COMPOUNDS:\n{湯|ゆ} (hot water, bath) + {冷|さ}め (getting cold)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nIn Japan, bathing culture emphasizes warming up fully in the bath. {湯冷|ゆざ}め is a common concern, especially:\n- In winter months\n- For children and elderly\n- After {温泉|おんせん} or {銭湯|せんとう}\n\nPREVENTION:\n- {髪|かみ}を{乾|かわ}かす - dry your hair\n- {体|からだ}をよく{拭|ふ}く - dry body thoroughly\n- {暖|あたた}かい{服|ふく}を{着|き}る - wear warm clothes\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {風邪|かぜ}を{引|ひ}く - to catch a cold\n- {寒気|さむけ} - feeling chilly\n- {湯上|ゆあ}がり - after bathing",
